Input: {"question": "Which league does Aldo Hudson play in?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 74, "text": "Here is a narrative that weaves in detailed evidence to support the claim:"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 76, "end": 189, "text": "It was a chilly winter evening in 1998 when Aldo Hudson stepped onto the court at Troy University's Trojan Arena."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 190, "end": 336, "text": "The crowd was electric, and the energy was palpable as the Trojans prepared to take on their arch-rivals, the University of South Alabama Jaguars."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 337, "end": 476, "text": "As a freshman guard, Aldo was about to make his debut in the NCAA Division I men's basketball league, and he was ready to make a statement."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 477, "end": 611, "text": "As the game tipped off, Aldo's quick reflexes and lightning-fast drives to the basket left the Jaguars' defense scrambling to keep up."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 612, "end": 730, "text": "His impressive performance that night, which included 17 points and 5 assists, was just a glimpse of what was to come."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 731, "end": 888, "text": "Over the course of the 1998-1999 season, Aldo would go on to establish himself as a force to be reckoned with in the NCAA Division I men's basketball league."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 889, "end": 974, "text": "But what exactly does it mean to play in the NCAA Division I men's basketball league?"}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 975, "end": 1059, "text": "For starters, it means competing against the best of the best in college basketball."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1060, "end": 1236, "text": "The NCAA, or National Collegiate Athletic Association, is the governing body for college athletics in the United States, and its Division I is the highest level of competition."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1237, "end": 1453, "text": "To be eligible to play in the NCAA Division I, a university must meet strict criteria, including a minimum number of athletic scholarships, a certain level of athletic budget, and a commitment to academic excellence."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1454, "end": 1553, "text": "Troy University, where Aldo played, is a member of the NCAA Division I and the Sun Belt Conference."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1554, "end": 1718, "text": "As a Division I school, Troy is required to adhere to the NCAA's strict rules and regulations, including those related to recruiting, eligibility, and athletic aid."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1719, "end": 1913, "text": "This means that Aldo, as a student-athlete at Troy, was subject to rigorous academic standards, including maintaining a minimum GPA and completing a certain number of credit hours each semester."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1914, "end": 2088, "text": "Throughout the 1998-1999 season, Aldo's impressive stats and clutch performances earned him recognition not only from his coaches and teammates but also from the NCAA itself."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2089, "end": 2205, "text": "He was named to the Sun Belt Conference All-Freshman Team, a testament to his hard work and dedication to the sport."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2206, "end": 2278, "text": "But Aldo's success on the court was not limited to individual accolades."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 181, "text": "As the sun dipped below the horizon, casting a warm orange glow over the campus of Troy University, Aldo Hudson laced up her sneakers and made her way to the Sartain Hall Gymnasium."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 182, "end": 364, "text": "It was a crisp autumn evening in 1998, and the air was alive with the hum of excitement as the Trojans prepared to take on their arch-rivals, the University of South Alabama Jaguars."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 365, "end": 506, "text": "Aldo, a junior point guard with a lightning-quick first step and a penchant for clutch three-pointers, was the undisputed leader of the team."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 507, "end": 647, "text": "Her coach, the wise and witty Karen Townsend, had often praised Aldo's exceptional court vision and ability to read the defense like a book."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 648, "end": 797, "text": "As Aldo took the court for warm-ups, she was greeted by the familiar sight of her teammates, each one a unique and vital cog in the Trojans' machine."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 798, "end": 1009, "text": "There was Rachel, the towering center with a soft touch and a mean streak; Jasmine, the speedy shooting guard with a flair for the dramatic; and Emily, the steady-handed power forward with a nose for rebounding."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1010, "end": 1142, "text": "Together, they formed a formidable unit, one that had been making waves in the NCAA Division I women's basketball league all season."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1143, "end": 1240, "text": "Aldo, in particular, had been turning heads with her impressive stats and fearless playing style."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1241, "end": 1336, "text": "She was the kind of player who could take over a game at any moment, and her opponents knew it."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1337, "end